+# Result: instrument-teeth — the predictions gate becomes a tool, not a reading
+
+**Project:** omegahive · **Order:** `orders/2026-07-29-instrument-teeth.md` · **Closed:** 2026-08-16
+
+## What shipped
+
+One `scripts/` PR (six files) plus RUNBOOK touches. All six scope items landed; the
+drill-hygiene fold is the two named classes only.
+
+- **`scripts/hive-common.sh`** — the shared Predictions parser, factored here as the single
+  source of truth for an order's `## Predictions` section:
+  - `parse_predictions <order-file>` sets `PRED_HAS_SECTION` / `PRED_DECLARED` / `PRED_FIELDS` /
+    `PRED_MISSING` / `PRED_OFFENDING` / the three `*_TXT` verbatim values. It reads the file's
+    text only; it never writes to the order (stop-line: tooling never edits an order body).
+  - `assess_predictions <order-file>` prints `refuse` | `warn` | `allow` — the gate's teeth.
+  - `PRED_LABELS` — the four literal bullet labels, printed by a refusal. `Named risks:` is
+    **reported** (printed) but never **counted** among the three scored fields (R9 held; a
+    gate-content change is the operator's call, not a worker's).
+  - `commit_metrics` **refuses rather than rebases** on push failure (scope 6): the commit stays
+    local, the manual resolution step is printed (`git pull --rebase && git push`), and the caller
+    returns non-zero. The old `push → pull --rebase → push` retry is gone.
+- **`scripts/hive-launch`** — the predictions gate (scope 1 + 2). Before any spine write, the
+  launch calls `assess_predictions` on the pinned order. A `## Predictions` section that is
+  present, carries no declared-unpredicted line, and parses none of the three scored fields
+  **refuses** — the message names the four literal labels, prints the offending lines, and names
+  `--anyway` as the deliberate escape. An absent section and the declared-unpredicted one-liner
+  launch cleanly; a 1–2-of-3 partial warns loudly and launches. Same parser `hive-score` uses.
+- **`scripts/hive-score`** — the same shared parser (scope 2 + 3); its own regex set is deleted.
+  Coverage now records **four distinct strings**: `unpredicted (no \`## Predictions\` section)`,
+  `unpredicted (declared unpredicted in section)`, `unpredicted (section present, 0 of 3 fields
+  parsed)`, and `partial (N of 3 fields predicted; missing: <labels>)` — so "nobody predicted"
+  and "the author predicted and we lost it" can never be conflated again (D1). `--review`
+  validates (scope 4): only `clean | minor rework | rework`, case-insensitive, stored lowercase;
+  anything else refuses with a message naming the three values.
+- **`scripts/hive-close`** — regenerates the project's `tasks.md`/`tasks.csv` alongside the score
+  (scope 5), retiring R6's surviving manual half. Same ordering discipline as scoring: strictly
+  after the close emits, strictly non-fatal, loud with the exact command to re-run.
+- **`scripts/hive-metrics-drill.sh`** — the deterministic leg. New fixture tasks (`theta` — the
+  `- **Effort:**` dialect, closed; plus `declared` and `twothirds` orders), and new sections:
+  the parser/gate predicate (refuse/warn/allow per fixture), the one-parser proof (the gate and
+  `hive-score` agree on the same input — DoD (c)), the `--review` validation, and the
+  `commit_metrics` refuses-not-rebases injection. Drill-hygiene sweep applied (see **Reflection**).
+- **`scripts/hive-tooling-drill.sh`** — new lifecycle cases (executed elsewhere, where the live
+  stack and tmux exist): the launch gate (refuse before provisioning, `--anyway`, declared/no-
+  section allow, 2-of-3 loud warn), close-regenerates-metrics assertions on the alpha close, and
+  an injected metrics-regeneration failure proving the close stands with a loud complaint.
+- **`workspace/projects/omegahive/RUNBOOK.md`** — operator surface updated: the predictions gate
+  under Launch, the close's metrics regeneration and `--review` vocabulary under Close, and the
+  Wave-close checklist now omits the retired `hive-metrics <project>` step.
+
+## How verified
+
+- **Hermetic drill green:** `bin/bench-verify -- scripts/hive-metrics-drill.sh` → **131 PASS,
+  0 FAIL**, no events issued, fixture byte-identical afterwards. This is the deterministic leg
+  and it covers every DoD letter that can be covered without the live stack:
+  - (a) `theta` order → `assess_predictions` = `refuse`; the refusal's raw material
+    (`PRED_FIELDS=0`, all three missing labels, offending lines captured) asserted;
+  - (b) `gamma` (no section) and `declared` → `allow`; `beta`/`twothirds` → `warn`;
+  - (c) the one-parser proof: `hive-score theta` records `section present, 0 of 3 fields parsed`
+    — the same parse the gate refuses on;
+  - (d) `gamma` and `theta` scored as the two distinct coverage strings on the same fixture;
+  - (e) `--review Rework` stores `rework`; `--review bogus` refuses naming the three values;
+  - (g) `commit_metrics` push-refusal: non-zero exit, loud, names `pull --rebase &&`, the local
+    commit survives, no `rebase failed` tell, recoverable by a plain push.
+- **`shellcheck -x` clean** on all six touched scripts (`hive-common.sh`, `hive-launch`,
+  `hive-score`, `hive-close`, `hive-metrics-drill.sh`, `hive-tooling-drill.sh`).
+- **The tooling drill was not run here** — it needs the live stack and tmux, which the task brief
+  executes elsewhere. Its new cases are written to the same assertion style as the existing ones
+  and cover DoD (a)/(b)/(f) end-to-end: launch refusal before any board state, `--anyway` launch,
+  declared/no-section clean launches, 2-of-3 loud warning, close-regenerates-metrics committed +
+  pushed, and the injected metrics-failure close-still-stands case.
+- No independent review ran (one bounded pass was not directed by the order; the drill cases are
+  the reviewable substance, per the order's own note that DoD (c) is "how review sees it").
+
+## To operate
+
+The operator surface changed in three places; the RUNBOOK carries the prose, the commands are:
+
+- **Launch a deliberately-unpredicted order after a refusal:** the refusal prints the four literal
+  labels and the offending lines. Either fix the labels to the literal forms (`Expected effort:`,
+  `Expected questions:`, `Expected review outcome:`, `Named risks:`) or launch deliberately
+  unpredicted with `hive-launch <order> --worker <id> --anyway`. An order with **no**
+  `## Predictions` section, or with the `- Declared unpredicted: …` one-liner, needs no `--anyway`.
+- **Wave close:** `hive-close <task>` now scores **and** regenerates the project's
+  `tasks.md`/`tasks.csv` — no separate `hive-metrics <project>` step. The `--review` verdict
+  remains the one field the spine cannot know: `hive-score <task> --review "<clean|minor rework|rework>" --again`
+  (three literal values only, case-insensitive, stored lowercase).
+- **Recovery for the two closed pln tasks whose labels R3 relabelled** (the order's named
+  operating step): re-score each to recover the two lost calibration data points:
+  ```bash
+  hive-score ptc-revalidate --project pln-benchmarks --again
+  hive-score pw-libpln-slice  --project pln-benchmarks --again
+  ```
+  Append `</dev/null` inside any loop (the spine read consumes stdin).
+- **Metrics push failure** (a new refusal, scope 6): `commit_metrics` now commits locally and
+  **refuses** to auto-rebase. Resolve by hand: `git -C <ops-ws> pull --rebase && git -C <ops-ws> push`.
+
+## Reflection
+
+- **The prose half failed exactly as D1 predicted, and the code half now cannot.** The
+  `- **Effort:**` dialect order `projects/pln-benchmarks/orders/2026-07-29-pw-writeup.md` was
+  caught at the wave-3 cut by a human doing the same reading that failed in wave 2. This order
+  makes that reading a launch gate with its own escape hatch, so the next author who re-words a
+  label gets a refusal that names the literal labels and prints the offending lines — not a
+  quiet `unpredicted` at scoring time. The gate is deliberately narrower than "has a Predictions
+  heading": absent and declared-unpredicted sections are recorded metrics, not errors, and the
+  refusal is on unparseable only.
+- **One parser, proven rather than asserted.** The reviewer's question for scope 2 was whether
+  the launch gate and the scorer are one parser or two that currently agree. The drill answers it
+  with a single input (`theta`) driven through both callers: the gate refuses it, the scorer
+  records it as section-present-unparsed. There is one regex set in the codebase and it lives in
+  `hive-common.sh`.
+- **`Named risks:` stayed unscored and got documented instead.** The order inherited R2's "N of 4"
+  vs the instrument's "3 scored fields" correction; the parser prints `Named risks:` among the
+  four literal labels but never counts it. That distinction is now in the code comment, the
+  launch-refusal message, and the RUNBOOK.
+- **Drill-hygiene sweep (DoD h), by class:**
+  - **Class 1 — EXIT-trap-before-isolation ordering.** `hive-metrics-drill.sh`: **none found** —
+    the drill is hermetic (no tmux, no live stack), its only cleanup is `rm -rf $SANDBOX`, which
+    has no default-socket hazard, so there is no isolation primitive whose ordering could bite.
+    `hive-tooling-drill.sh` already carries the fix (tmux isolation precedes the trap).
+  - **Class 2 — `cmd | grep -q` SIGPIPE under `set -o pipefail`.** `hive-metrics-drill.sh`:
+    **22 instances fixed** — every `grep -q*` at the right end of a pipeline changed to
+    `grep ... >/dev/null`, so a match no longer SIGPIPEs the producer (the passing case is
+    exactly when `-q` exits early). No rewrite, no restructure, no new framework — the fixes are
+    the one-token kind the order's bound allows. The remaining `grep -q` calls in the file are
+    direct file greps (not pipelines) and are unaffected.
+  - **No third class was found.** The boundary the order set ("a third defect class found is a
+    finding for the report, not a scope expansion") did not fire.
+- **A coverage string changed by the order's own wording.** `hive-score` previously recorded
+  `unpredicted (no usable \`## Predictions\` section)`; the order specifies
+  `unpredicted (no \`## Predictions\` section)`. The word "usable" is gone, and the two distinct
+  strings now match the order byte for byte.
+- **`--review` validation closes a real wave-2 column.** Retro 1's instrument note said lowercase
+  only, but wave 2 produced `Rework`, `Clean`, and `minor rework` into the same column. The
+  validator is three literal values, case-insensitive, stored lowercase — the column can no
+  longer drift back.
+- **The close→metrics coupling's blast radius is contained, twice.** The score-failure case
+  (already drilled) and the metrics-failure case (new) both prove the same discipline: the close
+  emits first, the follow-ups are non-fatal, and a broken remote leaves a loud complaint naming
+  exactly one recovery command. That the metrics step was added at all raises `commit_metrics`
+  firing rate — which is precisely why scope 6 (refuse, never rebase) rode in the same PR.
